## Exercise B

Draw a **LineString** between any two locations (minimum 2 clicks, double-click to finish). Export the result: `Save > GeoJSON`.

Paste the exported text into the code cell below and run it to confirm the structure — geometry type, coordinate count, and any properties you added.
import json

# Paste your exported GeoJSON string here (replace the placeholder)
exported = """
{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "features": []
}
"""

data = json.loads(exported)
print("Type:", data["type"])
print("Features:", len(data["features"]))
for f in data["features"]:
    print(" -", f["geometry"]["type"], "| properties:", f["properties"])
